<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>DiagnosticCatalog.BannedApi</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>DiagnosticCatalog.BannedApi</RootNamespace>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    This catalogue ships on the 'bannedapi' train, which versions independently of the foundation so
    it can follow Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.BannedApiAnalyzers' releases without dragging anything else
    along. Declaring the train here is the whole membership (Directory.Build.targets); it is also
    what makes the project packable, what gives it an embedded SBOM, and what puts the icon on the
    package.

    A train of its own rather than sharing 'roslyn' or 'publicapi'. All three packages ship from
    dotnet/roslyn-analyzers and version in lockstep today, but they are three NuGet packages a
    consumer installs separately, and sharing a train would tie a release of any one of them to the
    other two's changelogs.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ReleaseTrain>bannedapi</ReleaseTrain>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Label="Package">
    <PackageId>DiagnosticCatalog.BannedApi</PackageId>
    <DevelopmentDependency>false</DevelopmentDependency>
    <Title>DiagnosticCatalog.BannedApi</Title>
    <Description>The banned-API rules (RS0030, RS0031, RS0035) as strongly referenced constants, so that SuppressMessageAttribute takes compile-checked references instead of magic strings. Ids, categories, titles and help links are read from Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.BannedApiAnalyzers' own DiagnosticDescriptor instances. For any codebase banning an API in BannedSymbols.txt. Unofficial; not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft.</Description>
    <PackageTags>roslyn;analyzers;diagnostics;suppressmessage;bannedapi;banned-symbols;api-governance;code-analysis;catalog</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.en.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Authors>Reefact</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Reefact</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Reefact/diagnostic-catalog</PackageProjectUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    A PACKAGE reference, not a project one. The foundation rides the 'lib' train and this catalogue
    rides its own, so packing against the project would stamp a dependency on a lib version that was
    never published, and every consumer's restore would fail with NU1102 on an immutable artifact
    (ADR-0007).

    Version-less, so it resolves from Directory.Packages.props — where moving every catalogue onto a
    new foundation is one deliberate edit rather than thirteen.

    NOT PrivateAssets="all": the foundation must reach whoever consumes this catalogue. They need
    [DiagnosticRule] resolvable to declare rules of their own, and present at run time for reflection
    over a catalogue to work (specification §16.1).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="DiagnosticCatalog" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.en.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
